// `:Debug` on a value with no Debug form is E0112. Its Fix never offers a
// spelling that fails for the same value: an `Iter<String>` has no `Display`
// either and Core owns it, so neither `{words}` nor an `impl` is offered.
run: fn() {
    words: "a,b".split(",")
    print("couldn't read {words:Debug}")
}
